      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "align": null,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "erwin wurm is not just ",
          "marks": {},
          "link": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "the son of a detective who did not like artists",
          "marks": {},
          "link": {
            "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erwin_Wurm",
            "record": null
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ", he is an artist who is still making ",
          "marks": {},
          "link": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "one-minute sculptures",
          "marks": {},
          "link": {
            "href": "https://www.erwinwurm.com/artworks/one-minute-sculptures",
            "record": null
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " decades after they inspired mark romanek to have members of the red hot chili peppers do headstands in buckets and sing in tubes. because it is often when i see something that inspires me that i come to find that the artist has long left this bitch of a planet (earth), it was very nice to see that erwin wurm is still around and challenging the meaning of sculpture. it was also very nice to read that he was properly compensated and credited being the inspiration of the video.",
          "marks": {},
          "link": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "align": "center",
      "kind": "image",
      "image": {
        "url": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:x5leeami62gbmjekf7ro6sqo/bafkreiagycqqtscbgr3huubn2mfkk3crrt2s2hqxj6awqkr23sfyvidubu@jpeg",
        "alt": "HORVAT How did you feel when you first saw\nthe music video for “Can’t Stop” by the Red Hot\nChili Peppers?\nWURM Great, because it was done with my\npermission. We set up a contract, I got paid, and\neverything was very professional. Also, I was cred-\nited as an artist, and I think that may have been\nthe first time an artist was credited for something\nin a mainstream music video. Many videos were\nplaying on MTV, but producers stole the ideas\nfrom other artists. “Can’t Stop” was done with my\npermission, and, in the end, it was an enormous\nadvertisement for my work.",
        "title": null,
        "aspectRatio": {
          "width": 1116,
          "height": 856
        },
        "width": {
          "value": 500,
          "unit": "px"
        },
        "fullBleed": false
      },
      "caption": null
    },
    {
      "align": null,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "from ",
          "marks": {
            "italic": true
          },
          "link": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "katya horvat's interview of erwin wurm in autre",
          "marks": {
            "italic": true
          },
          "link": {
            "href": "https://www.erwinwurm.com/fileadmin/user_upload/Periodicals/2021/Autre.pdf",
            "record": null
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ". and ",
          "marks": {
            "italic": true
          },
          "link": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "this is another interview",
          "marks": {
            "italic": true
          },
          "link": {
            "href": "https://www.culturedmag.com/article/2023/11/22/erwin-wurm-artist-show-scad/",
            "record": null
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": " where he talks about getting that call.",
          "marks": {
            "italic": true
          },
          "link": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "align": null,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "what a bummer that i simply assumed that wurm had no involvement in the video - that's just how used to seeing ideas stolen i've become over my time on the internet. i've had ideas and credit stolen a lot over my career and the worst part about it is the frustration that ferments as i play through the moments when i had to decide if it's worth calling out or not. writing this is making me play through them again and i don't like that! anyway, i don't know if this move was straight out of mark romanek's values framework or if someone else told him he had to do the right thing, but regardless this was a cool thing to learn about.",
          "marks": {},
          "link": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "align": null,
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "so, that was my \"can't stop\" post. if this was a nice thing for you to learn about and you learned about it from me by reading these words that i wrote with my own brain, i appreciate your support by sharing this, following me elsewhere and maybe throwing a few bucks in my ",
          "marks": {},
          "link": null
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "purple hippo (?) mascot head-shaped bank.",
          "marks": {},
          "link": {
            "href": "https://ko-fi.com/jennschiffer",
            "record": null
          }
        }
      ]
    }
